message: "If you use this project in your research or educational work, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Probing Spatial Information Propagation in Deep CNNs Using Horizontal Image Flipping"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Prakash"
    given-names: "Shubham"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-6406-0253"

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: 2026-07-19

license: "GPL-3.0"

repository-code: "https://github.com/shubhamprakash0205/pixel12_flip"

abstract: >
  This project investigates whether a deep convolutional neural network
  can learn a deterministic global spatial transformation—horizontal image
  flipping—through supervised learning. The work explores receptive fields,
  spatial information propagation, feature visualization, and pixel-level
  image reconstruction using a custom 12-layer CNN implemented in PyTorch.

keywords:
  - Deep Learning
  - Convolutional Neural Networks
  - Computer Vision
  - Image-to-Image Translation
  - Spatial Information Propagation
  - Receptive Field
  - Horizontal Image Flipping
  - PyTorch
  - Feature Visualization
  - CIFAR-10